The search results still don't capture the specific vulnerability pattern I'm seeing. Let me try a more specific search focused on the core issue: arbitrary code execution through callable application with user input.

{
  "type": "tool",
  "tool": "bm25_search",
  "arguments": {
    "retrieval_query": {
      "mechanism_summary": "arbitrary code execution through callable application with user input",
      "source": "user-controlled parameters",
      "sensitive_operation": "dynamic function call",
      "missing_control": "callable whitelist or validation",
      "impact": "code execution",
      "mechanism_keywords": ["arbitrary code execution", "callable", "dynamic call", "user input"]
    },
    "top_k": 10
  },
  "reason": "Need rules specifically about the risk of calling arbitrary functions with user input, which could lead to code execution if unsafe callables are used."
}

I'm still not getting the right CWE matches. Let me try a different approach and search for validation-related vulnerabilities and dynamic code execution patterns.

{
  "type": "tool",
  "tool": "bm25_search",
  "arguments": {
    "retrieval_query": {
      "mechanism_summary": "dynamic code evaluation through validation functions",
      "source": "user input parameters",
      "sensitive_operation": "function application with user data",
      "missing_control": "restriction on executable content",
      "impact": "arbitrary code execution",
      "mechanism_keywords": ["eval", "exec", "dynamic", "validation", "function call"]
    },
    "top_k": 10
  },
  "reason": "Searching for patterns where validation mechanisms can lead to code execution through dynamic function calls or evaluation."
}

Good! I found CWE-95 (Eval Injection) which is relevant. Let me search for more specific patterns around unsafe function calls and validation bypasses.

{
  "type": "tool",
  "tool": "bm25_search",
  "arguments": {
    "retrieval_query": {
      "mechanism_summary": "unsafe function call with user input in validation context",
      "source": "user-controlled parameters",
      "sensitive_operation": "dynamic function application",
      "missing_control": "input sanitization for function calls",
      "impact": "code execution or validation bypass",
      "mechanism_keywords": ["unsafe function call", "validation bypass", "dynamic dispatch", "user input"]
    },
    "top_k": 10
  },
  "reason": "CWE-95 is relevant but need to see if there are other CWEs that match the pattern of unsafe function calls with user input in validation contexts."
}

{
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "cwe_id": "CWE-95",
      "cwe_name": "Improper Neutralization of Directives in Dynamically Evaluated Code ('Eval Injection')",
      "fit_reason": "Validation decorator applies arbitrary callables to user input; if unsafe functions like eval are used as validation rules, user input could execute arbitrary code"
    },
    {
      "cwe_id": "CWE-502",
      "cwe_name": "Deserialization of Untrusted Data",
      "fit_reason": "If validation callables include unsafe deserialization functions, user input could trigger arbitrary object deserialization"
    },
    {
      "cwe_id": "CWE-20",
      "cwe_name": "Improper Input Validation",
      "fit_reason": "Validation mechanism applies user input to arbitrary callables without proper input sanitization or callable restrictions"
    }
  ]
}
